# Sanitized structural-union fixture for the Netdata Ceph Prometheus profile.
# Ceph 18 source: ceph/ceph @ efac5a54607c13fa50d4822e50242b86e6e446df.
# Ceph 19 source: ceph/ceph @ abc7aa7f2701e5d46878fd5e6bb7e2955f1a395a.
# Ceph 20 source: ceph/ceph @ 0fcffee29411e3a38036764817b6e1afc59741cc.
# NVMe-oF source: ceph/ceph-nvmeof @ c79b6f44bd2288f7ec5c48e3cc47f6e566573d3f.
# Combines MGR, official ceph-exporter daemon roles, release-specific scrub contracts,
# and source-backed optional CephFS/MDS, RBD/PWL, RBD Mirror, RGW multisite/topic, runtime transport,
# memory-pool, SimpleRADOSStriper, and NVMe-oF surfaces.
# Values and identities are synthetic; no live endpoints, hostnames, FSIDs, or customer data are present.
# Includes source-defined priority-0 daemon counters and conditional ceph-exporter process metrics.
# Added optional-source registrations are traced to src/rgw/rgw_dmclock_scheduler_ctx.cc,
# src/tools/cephfs_mirror/{Mirror,FSMirror,PeerReplayer}.cc, src/kv/rocksdb_cache/BinnedLRUCache.{cc,h},
# src/client/Client.cc, src/extblkdev/fcm/ExtBlkDevPluginFcm.cc, and src/osdc/Objecter.cc at the Ceph 20 revision above.
# NVMe-oF's control/prometheus.py uses prometheus/client_python 0.19.0 and unregisters its GC collector;
# the fixture retains that registry's process/platform families but not Python GC families.
